  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let the equation of plane passing through the line&nbsp;of intersection of the planes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8484;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;if the distance of this plane from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>",
